      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Saint Johns was originally called Tsézhin Deezʼáhí by Navajo people, a name that reflects the area's striking rock formations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
